      "id": 1,
      "text": "Falls Mill Bridge, linking West Logan to Logan via Ohio State Route 664, takes its name from the historic Falls Mill that once powered the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Logan%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Columbus Washboard Company, the only remaining washboard manufacturer in the United States, still hand‑crafts vintage‑style washboards in its quirky downtown factory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.explorehockinghills.com/visit-historic-downtown-logan/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Hocking County Historical and Genealogical Society & Museum, housed in a historic building, offers exhibits that trace Hocking County’s journey from pioneer days to today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.explorehockinghills.com/visit-historic-downtown-logan/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Bowen House, a stately 19th‑century home turned cultural arts center, hosts rotating art exhibits, music performances, and community workshops amid historic charm.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.explorehockinghills.com/visit-historic-downtown-logan/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "West Logan sits on the Hocking River, nestled between the city limits of Logan and the U.S. Route 23 corridor.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Logan%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Historic downtown West Logan has been revitalized, with restored buildings, bustling sidewalks, and colorful flowerbeds that bring new life to every corner.",
